  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 241 AM CDT Sat Oct 24 2026\n\nThere's not a lot to speak on for this weekend as our stretch \nof dry, mild weather continues. Temperatures early this morning \nare in the 40s and 50s with mostly clear skies now giving way to\na high cloud deck filling in from the west. Some patchy fog is \nbeginning to blossom around parts of SE WI and north-central IN.\nPatchy coverage is expected to spread into portions of our CWA \nprior to daybreak, primarily across parts of NW Indiana as well \nas in Lake Co, IL. While dense fog is not a widespread concern, \nlocalized pockets of some denser fog will certainly be possible \nthrough early morning, especially in Lake Co, IL. Otherwise, \nexpect another pleasant late October day today with highs \nforecast in the lower 70s and a fair mix of mid-high clouds and \nsunshine.\n\nTomorrow is anticipated to be slightly warmer with lower to \nmiddle 70s in the forecast. A weakly-forced cold front will drop\nthrough the area from the north late Sunday into Monday. While \nwe're not expecting any rain out of this, it will cool things \noff slightly for Monday and Tuesday. Monday, given that the \nfront will be pushing north to south across our area into the \ndaytime, is expected to see high temperatures range from the \nlower and middle 60s in our north to the 70 farther south. 60s \nand lower 70s will persist through the week with rain-free \nconditions favored through at least mid-week. A series of waves \nis then progged to traverse the region and possibly provide us \nwith some rain late in the week and into next weekend. \n\nDoom",
